== made against the current ancestry ==
branches: 1 next=2
  * br-1 Robust @sec-3  {threshold=0.95}
== a change BELOW the branch point leaves it alone ==
branches: 1 next=2
  * br-1 Robust @sec-3  {threshold=0.95}
stale: 0
== a change ABOVE it does not ==
branches: 1 next=2
  * br-1 Robust @sec-3  [ancestry changed]  {threshold=0.95}
stale: 1
and it is still SELECTED — the flag is surfaced, not acted on:
  selected=br-1
== re-anchoring is explicit: a person looked and accepted ==
-> reanchor: reanchored br-1
branches: 1 next=2
  * br-1 Robust @sec-3  {threshold=0.95}
